{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions","id":1139469,"title":"Soul Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-11T09:34:36-07:00","id":1139469,"title":"Soul Questions","content":"Are souls really as interchangeable as the rules make it seem? If you use Death to swap Alice's and Bob's souls around, will there be any side effects? Do we know if there are side effects that crop up after you die?<br /> <br /> Do animals have souls? If not, what happens if I turn a cat into a human with Life 4? Does the transformed cat suffer soul loss? What if I used Mind 3 to boost the cat's intelligence to human levels? What if I also used the Life 3 Mutation spell repeatedly to turn the cat into something that looked fairly human? Would it need a soul then?<br /> <br /> Do other supernatural beings have souls? Vampires? Mummies? Demons? What does a Werewolf, Changeling, or Beast soul look like? What would happen if a Mage gave a soul to a Promethian? <br /> <br /> Is a soul necessary for moral action? If you use magic to create a sentient construct, does it get a virtue and morality track without a soul? Can you give a soul to a spirit? If so, what happens?<br /> <br /> If a soul isn't necessary for moral action and it's not what makes you yourself, what exactly is it? What is the point of the soul? Are humans spiritually crippled because we need this extra booster for us to stay sane? Is it a symbol of our connection to the Supernal Realms?<br /> <br /> And I get that canon is unlikely to specify answers to all of these questions and that many of them are probably good Mysteries to explore in play, but I currently kinda feel like I don't really &quot;get&quot; souls so any thoughts you might have will be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 09-11-2017, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T09:57:10-07:00","id":1139473,"title":"","content":"Yes souls are swappable.<br /> <br /> A cat turned into a human needs a soul is how I'd rule it. A cat that has had Transformation cast repeatedly on it does not, it's a cat with human qualities grafted on.<br /> <br /> Other supernaturals appear to have something that approximates as a soul. It's unclear if it's the same or can be removed.<br /> <br /> A soul isn't necessary for moral action, also there isn't a morality track for any splat. A sentient construct doesn't receive an Integrity track or its equivalent. Depending on the kind of construct, a ghost for instance, it might get a virtue.<br /> <br /> Your second to last paragraph can only be answered by the ST of your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T10:27:40-07:00","id":1139480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions#post1139469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are souls really as interchangeable as the rules make it seem? If you use Death to swap Alice's and Bob's souls around, will there be any side effects? Do we know if there are side effects that crop up after you die?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are, but important to know that the soul isn't the mind or essence of the person the way we usually think of it. The soul is more like the engine that keeps the person the running, without it they can keep going, but eventually they'll run down into a husk. You can swap Bob and Alice's souls, and they're fine. It's like swapping the engines between cars. After you die your soul isn't what remains hanging around, the soul goes away when you die, what hangs around as a ghost or goes to the Underworld is different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do animals have souls? If not, what happens if I turn a cat into a human with Life 4? Does the transformed cat suffer soul loss? What if I used Mind 3 to boost the cat's intelligence to human levels? What if I also used the Life 3 Mutation spell repeatedly to turn the cat into something that looked fairly human? Would it need a soul then? </div> </div> </div>They don't have souls as far as I know. It sounds like you still have an animal without a soul, it's just smarter and looks more like a person than a house cat. Inside, it's still an animal though. It could be an interesting, and wildly unethical, experiment a Mage (or Archmaster) could be running. Trying to find the line that defines humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do other supernatural beings have souls? Vampires? Mummies? Demons? What does a Werewolf, Changeling, or Beast soul look like? What would happen if a Mage gave a soul to a Promethian? </div> </div> </div>I'm less sure about this one different game lines look at this different ways, other people probably know more.<ul><li>Vampires: I don't think they have souls, the Beast taking it's place.</li> <li>Mummies: I haven't read Mummy.</li> <li>Demons: No, they aren't human, and never were human. When they make a deal with a mortal to take their soul, they don't actually take the soul.</li> <li>Werewolf: I haven't really read Werewolf, but I suspect they don't have a soul the way humans have them. They're part spirit and part flesh, and children of ancient gods, so I suspect they're more integrated and there isn't some definable soul you could remove. The flesh and spirit is mixed together, not two distinct and separate halves.</li> <li>Changeling: There is a new edition coming out for this line, so things might change. 1E was kinda cagey as to if Changelings still had souls or not, but the general impression was that they had a soul, but it was tattered and broken and the hollows filled with things from Arcadia and the Hedge.</li> <li>Beast: I think the Horror devours a Beast's soul when they become a Beast, and afterwards the Horror fulfills the same functions as the soul.</li> <li>Promethean: I suspect giving a Promethean a soul would be like tying a balloon to something that is on fire. The string is going to burn up and the balloon is going to float away no matter how many times you do it. The Promethean isn't ready for a soul yet, and there is a fire where the soul would go.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is a soul necessary for moral action? If you use magic to create a sentient construct, does it get a virtue and morality track without a soul? Can you give a soul to a spirit? If so, what happens? </div> </div> </div>2nd Edition moves away from away from tracking moral action for most splats, or humans. Lacking a soul doesn't prevent you from taking moral action, and doesn't really have anything to do with Virtue or Vice (unless you had a soul and lost it). Plenty of things that don't have souls have a Virtue and Vice (angels, Demons, spirits, soulless humans, etc...). Most spirits can't do anything with a soul, you could try and attach it to the spirit with magic, but they wouldn't interact with each other. Some spirits can do things with souls, but more as a commodity, they don't integrate teh soul with themselves or anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a soul isn't necessary for moral action and it's not what makes you yourself, what exactly is it? What is the point of the soul? Are humans spiritually crippled because we need this extra booster for us to stay sane? Is it a symbol of our connection to the Supernal Realms? </div> </div> </div>A symbol of our connection to the Supernal Realms is a excellent description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I get that canon is unlikely to specify answers to all of these questions and that many of them are probably good Mysteries to explore in play, but I currently kinda feel like I don't really &quot;get&quot; souls so any thoughts you might have will be appreciated. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T16:55:33-07:00","id":1139583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions#post1139469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are souls really as interchangeable as the rules make it seem? If you use Death to swap Alice's and Bob's souls around, will there be any side effects? Do we know if there are side effects that crop up after you die?</div> </div> </div> </div>For all intents and purposes, yes, they seem to be that interchangeable. Noticeable side effects may occur, but they may not. It's hard to tell which is freakier. As for what happens when you die... No-one really knows either way. There might not actually be an afterlife in Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions#post1139469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do animals have souls? If not, what happens if I turn a cat into a human with Life 4? Does the transformed cat suffer soul loss? What if I used Mind 3 to boost the cat's intelligence to human levels? What if I also used the Life 3 Mutation spell repeatedly to turn the cat into something that looked fairly human? Would it need a soul then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Animals lack individual souls in the same manner humans have them. Turn a cat into a human with Life 4, it remains mentally and spiritually a cat. If you gave it greater intellect, it would still be, spiritually, a cat. Probably. Who knows? But that spiritual element that makes humans human would not be present, nor would it likely be missed. What's there would be obviously not human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions#post1139469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do other supernatural beings have souls? Vampires? Mummies? Demons? What does a Werewolf, Changeling, or Beast soul look like? What would happen if a Mage gave a soul to a Promethian?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have something soul-like in most cases. Demons do not, because they're not even remotely close to human; they do a good job of <i>pretending</i> to be, but a Demon isn't human. A Demon is essentially a player in an RPG; they pretend to be someone they aren't, even get emotionally invested in it, but they're going to drop the act the moment it stops being worthwhile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions#post1139469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a soul necessary for moral action? If you use magic to create a sentient construct, does it get a virtue and morality track without a soul? Can you give a soul to a spirit? If so, what happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, a soul isn't a prerequisite to be moral or feel compassion, nor does having a soul guarantee you'll be or feel either. If you create a sentient construct, it having virtues or morality entirely depend on whether you choose to give it them. If you give a spirit a soul, it will eat it. Spirits lack a metaphysical &quot;slot&quot; for a soul to sit in, and forcibly creating one and jamming a soul in would have highly unpredictable results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions#post1139469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a soul isn't necessary for moral action and it's not what makes you yourself, what exactly is it? What is the point of the soul? Are humans spiritually crippled because we need this extra booster for us to stay sane? Is it a symbol of our connection to the Supernal Realms?</div> </div> </div> </div>The soul, to the best of my understanding, is sort of like a foundation to a person's being. It's not their mind, their connection to the Supernal, their body, their connection to the ephemeral... But it's the things without which none of those exist. It's sort of like a psychic support structure; the scaffold used to build everything else. Without it, everything kind of starts drifting on autopilot, before finally starting to crumble away until nothing remains. A person, one might say, is the metaphysical reality the soul extrudes and exudes around itself. You need a soul like you need a heart; you can get a transplant and survive just fine, but, without one, you can't really live.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions#post1139469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I get that canon is unlikely to specify answers to all of these questions and that many of them are probably good Mysteries to explore in play, but I currently kinda feel like I don't really &quot;get&quot; souls so any thoughts you might have will be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>The easiest way to think about it is to stop thinking of it as a soul. That's a really loaded word that's taken on baggage with time; baggage not reflected in Mage's setting. The soul here is more of an... Elan vital. It isn't what keeps you alive or lets you feel emotions or defines your spiritual aspect, but it's the thing which makes all those possible; as if your ability to feel emotions or drive or higher virtue and lower vice are cups that need to constantly be filled by an outpouring from some higher source. Make of the implications there what you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T02:45:44-07:00","id":1139665,"title":"","content":"As we see from legacies, a soul is really just a blob of energy. All it's &quot;features&quot; are a product of the vessel.<br /> <br /> Everyone has a sort of &quot;soul container&quot; that's a particular shape. Legacies can change it, and supernaturals might have something else filling it, but ultimately who you are is a function of your mind<i>, </i>not your soul.<br /> <br /> I think ephemeral beings were once described as being characterised by having a mind, body and soul that was all the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T06:40:19-07:00","id":1139696,"title":"","content":"Its counter to 2E canon but from 1E there were signs that your soul was kind unique in Creation. Merits like Ancient Echoes or Destiny pointed that your own soul is <b><i>designed</i></b> to be 'your-your' soul - only that you can eschew this is shining new immortality or powers of souls being more important to you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I still sustain this ruling in my games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T09:14:04-07:00","id":1139716,"title":"","content":"I recommend reading <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/764484-what-do-souls-really-give-you\">this thread</a>, as it tries to explain the metaphysics of souls from a systems perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T13:54:17-07:00","id":1140002,"title":"","content":"From this perspective, I kinda feel like they should have used a different word than &quot;soul&quot; as it has a lot of baggage that comes with it. It creates confusion if you just ignore said baggage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T18:01:04-07:00","id":1140050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1140002#post1140002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From this perspective, I kinda feel like they should have used a different word than &quot;soul&quot; as it has a lot of baggage that comes with it. It creates confusion if you just ignore said baggage.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the culture I grew up and am living in doesn't associate the word for 'soul' with morality or sentience, and is much closer to the elan vital as Axelgear described. Nor does it describe the soul as an indivisible thing. (By the way, I'm referring to the Taoist / Northeast Asian shamanistic concept of the soul.)<br /> <br /> So it seems players' and the writers' cultural backgrounds and research materials have to do with whether we consider something baggage or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T19:49:47-07:00","id":1140067,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the idea of a soul as some detachable ephemeral notion of &quot;You&quot; is not universal. It's definitely the most common notion in the West but, again, not universal by any means. Even the Genesis narrative's most common English translations use soul as a term for what happens when you combine clay with the breath of life; a soul being a living person, which ceases to exist when the breath leaves the clay.<br /> <br /> Once you move past the baggage, it gets easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T20:49:42-07:00","id":1140417,"title":"","content":"I kind of like using the soul as an ephemeral notion of 'You'. But not, like, the You that other people can see or interact with. Your I.<br /> Thing is, from an in setting perspective that makes it kind of difficult to prove that it actually serves that purpose. If you lose your soul and replace it with someone else's, it's not like you can tell the difference really. It doesn't have your memory, or your personality, though it is possible for bits and pieces of both to come through in the transplant. Most things have a soul-equivalent, but those who lack one entirely are basically P-Zombies.<br /> I've been considering using a Houserule which connects a player to their character's soul, such that if it's lost they lose control and if it ends up in someone else they start playing that character instead. Naturally, this means that I wouldn't bring up soul loss too often in my Chronicles, but it might be a fun way to add weight to the soul and provoke existential crises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T02:33:11-07:00","id":1140459,"title":"","content":"It's been my assumption that souls are molded by the people they're in and only preserve a shape upon undergoing the transformative process of death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T10:19:09-07:00","id":1141106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1140459#post1140459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been my assumption that souls are molded by the people they're in and only preserve a shape upon undergoing the transformative process of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if another comparison might be to a hard-drive. The actual disk isn't important, the data on it is. You can swap out drives and put the same data on them (and the disks can store the data from the system they were once connected to). You still need <i>a</i> hard-drive to persist the data (once out of memory), but which one isn't so important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T11:53:19-07:00","id":1141147,"title":"","content":"Ghosts aren't souls. 2E makes this very clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:09:51-07:00","id":1141179,"title":"","content":"Do animals possess souls in the setting?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:14:57-07:00","id":1141181,"title":"","content":"No, animals cast spirit reflections. Only human (or near human) beings posess souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:45:12-07:00","id":1141188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1141181#post1141181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, animals cast spirit reflections. Only human (or near human) beings posess souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then what the anima mundi is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:51:29-07:00","id":1141193,"title":"","content":"While the Astral Realms are called personal soul, soul of humanity and world soul it has remarkedly little to do with actual souls. It seems mostly humanity has access to it and that may well be connected to them having souls, but in the end a whole bunch of soulless stuff runs around in the astral (like every single goetia).<br /> <br /> But good question, no idea how the anima mundis existence is justified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T13:51:48-07:00","id":1141194,"title":"","content":"To be honest I kinda find that soul business kinda confusing, sure many other cultures have a different conception of the soul but most still have something that is REALLY you and will exist in some form of afterlife, the most common difference just being that this is is only one of several spiritual components of a being and sometimes not even the only sapient one.<br /> Even the few religions denying the existence of souls or the self for philosophical reasons such as buddhism only reject the notion of an unchanging and eternal you, in practice almost all buddhists believe in reincarnation (most buddhists are actually lay members of the religion hoping to be reborn as monks) and few believe that Nirvana is really oblivion.<br /> And obviously, people don't really like religions without an afterlife for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> I don't really get what is *you* in Chronicles of Darkness metaphysics, like are *you* that souless thing that remains once you lose your soul? It's hard to care about what happens to your soul after death if you are not your soul and kinda makes it hard to hate lichs if the only alternative is oblivion.<br /> Or are *you* the soul but memories and personality are not in the soul (souless beings are philosophical zombies)? It's very horrifying if your original soul is destroyed even if you get a new one because then you are just someone with the personality and the memories of someone else, NOT a guy with a new soul.<br /> <br /> On the same subject, is anything stated about what happens to the Gnosis of a Mage when he dies? I've read something about the &quot;spark&quot; of a mage dying when he dies even if ghost mages are maybe somewhat contradicting that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T14:00:59-07:00","id":1141200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1141147#post1141147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts aren't souls. 2E makes this very clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's that got to do with anything that's been said? No one suggested they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T14:41:29-07:00","id":1141215,"title":"","content":"So what exactly did you mean here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1140459#post1140459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been my assumption that souls are molded by the people they're in and only preserve a shape upon undergoing the transformative process of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T14:46:53-07:00","id":1141217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1141188#post1141188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then what the anima mundi is?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/949535-open-dev-signs-of-sorcery-sheer-perfection?p=950625#post950625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Anima Mundi is the collective soul of everything that doesn't have a soul. Yes, this makes sense.<br /> <br /> Well kinda. If you think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\">characterlimit</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T14:50:28-07:00","id":1141218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1141193#post1141193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But good question, no idea how the anima mundis existence is justified.</div> </div> </div> </div>A possible explanation could be that as the Temenos corresponds to the interior of the soul (or human souls collectively) so the Anima Mundi corresponds to the interior of the Shadow. I don't think that's really the authorial intent, but it's a possibility if you want to be neat about it.<br /> Also, at least in 1e (probably 2e too, but I'd need to check), going to Wisdom 0 means you lost access to the Temenos which would seem to indicate that there's more than just a similarity of terminology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't really get what is *you* in Chronicles of Darkness metaphysics, like are *you* that souless thing that remains once you lose your soul? </div> </div> </div>It's a good question. I don't think it's ever been explicitly stated, but the CofD seem to mirror reality in a strange way. There are souls and weird cosmologies, but fundamentally, the question of personal identity is as up in the air as it is in reality. Actually maybe even more so as the Awakening causes Magi to radically alter their perception of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T15:05:48-07:00","id":1141221,"title":"","content":"There was also a suggestion made a while back that the shadow might <i>be </i>the temenos of the world, more or less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T15:11:37-07:00","id":1141223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1141215#post1141215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what exactly did you mean here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that Death is a transformative process which leaves a permanent imprint of &quot;you&quot; on a soul in a way that it doesn't retain during the course of your life. It's a theory that explains the importance of souls beyond simply allowing you to avoid the Thrall Condition while leaving souls swappable, and also explains the persistent belief of death being a transitory state that takes you to a new plane of existence or prepares you for reincarnation.<br /> <br /> The idea that souls are moldable by the experiences of the body it's housed in also jives with Legacies, which are a deliberate perversion of a natural process by Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T15:48:36-07:00","id":1141235,"title":"","content":"I always thought the Anima Mundi is the collective soul of everything that doesn't have an individual soul. What Dave said quite some time ago (quoted by Satchel above) strengthened this. <br /> <br /> Of course this is confusing to anyone who thought souls are a unique thing to each person. Not so much to people who thought otherwise. In Hinduism, individual souls (atman) are still a part of the universal existence (brahman), with the key to enlightenment being realizing that. Buddhism goes a step further and outright says that the notion of an individual, singular, and everlasting soul/self is an illusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T15:59:43-07:00","id":1141240,"title":"","content":"That does fit with the view of the astral as a whole as a big sort of tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T23:40:25-07:00","id":1141331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1141106#post1141106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if another comparison might be to a hard-drive. The actual disk isn't important, the data on it is. You can swap out drives and put the same data on them (and the disks can store the data from the system they were once connected to). You still need <i>a</i> hard-drive to persist the data (once out of memory), but which one isn't so important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking indications from 1E cosmology, I would go with this analogy even further - your original soul (hard drive) was built to be <i>explicity</i> made for you (computer), but you <b>can</b> run with other souls (other hard drives). They just won't be as effective ( not having proper Destiny or Soul Echoes ). And some other drawbacks can show sometime...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-18-2017, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T23:40:26-07:00","id":1141330,"title":"","content":"Double post, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T15:56:32-07:00","id":1141567,"title":"","content":"Expanding on my theory that a soul imprints at death, ghosts then are probably a misfire of that metaphysical mechanism. Instead of imprinting the soul it imprints the Essence generated by the death, and being Essence instead of a soul the ghost is an imperfect copy of the individual. Their soul moves on unimprinted. Maybe when a ghost is resolved in the way that doesn't result in going to the Underworld it manages to fix the imprint mechanism and becomes the dead soul or takes the imprint to the dead soul resulting in the dead person experiencing what humans are supposed to experience after death.<br /> <br /> Dying soulless and not leaving a ghost would be a pretty effective way to keep from ever experiencing whatever passes for the afterlife or reincarnation.<br /> <br /> So, if ghosts are what happens when the Death part of your soul glitches, I wonder what results from the other four parts breaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-19-2017, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T13:38:22-07:00","id":1141877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1141567#post1141567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expanding on my theory that a soul imprints at death, ghosts then are probably a misfire of that metaphysical mechanism. Instead of imprinting the soul it imprints the Essence generated by the death, and being Essence instead of a soul the ghost is an imperfect copy of the individual. Their soul moves on unimprinted. Maybe when a ghost is resolved in the way that doesn't result in going to the Underworld it manages to fix the imprint mechanism and becomes the dead soul or takes the imprint to the dead soul resulting in the dead person experiencing what humans are supposed to experience after death.<br /> <br /> Dying soulless and not leaving a ghost would be a pretty effective way to keep from ever experiencing whatever passes for the afterlife or reincarnation.<br /> <br /> So, if ghosts are what happens when the Death part of your soul glitches, I wonder what results from the other four parts breaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually an interesting idea. It goes well with my theory that Death is to the Gross Arcana what Prime is to the Arcana as a whole. Prime is a language that describes all of the Arcana, including itself. On the other hand, what is the primary difference between a given Gross and Subtle Arcanum? The Gross arcanum is more percise, more easily measurable, more <i>definite</i>. For example, the Fate Arcanum contains all of the possible timelines and possibilities, while Time deals with a specific timeline, defined by its &quot;borders&quot; (endings) from the rest of potential time. In a sense, Death <b>is</b> the idea of Gross Arcana, a meta-Arcanum of all Gross Arcana. Matter is then the Arcanum reflecting the idea of Death as represented by the Material. It's an Arcanum that doesn't act, but is acted upon and it's surprisingly stable, as the Matter 2 Attainment shows.<br /> <br /> This would explain, why would Death be so important to the imprinting process. Death would pretty much function as an Arcanum, by which reality can know itself through the process of limitation of a given Subtle Arcanum and a subsequent Soul imprinting of those limitations into the essence (not Essence) of the Death Arcanum.<br /> <br /> Also, it's worth mentioning, that one thing unique to humans in the Astral is the Temenos, the collective soul of humanity. Animals (or other creatures) don't have it. And one unique landmark of Temenos marking its border is the Omphalos stone, considered to be an Artifact that was at some point put there. It's possible that the whole imprinting process and the reason humans have individual Souls is because it's been somehow artificially encoded into the Omphalos, and maybe the Temenos as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 09-19-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:21:30-07:00","id":1141968,"title":"","content":"If that's the case then the Omphalos were certainly established in the Time Before since it seems to be an irrevocable part of human history that can't be erased by the Exarchs. Maybe a break in the Mind function of the soul would result in a loss to the Temenos in a way that isn't as much of a breakdown or is lateral to the Soulless and subsequent Conditions. Something like Nebuchadnezzar perhaps, where a human isn't necessarily insane but reverts to a sort of animal existence after being cut off from the rest of humanity. I dunno, definitely seems like something worth exploring as a thought experiment though. Ghosts are a fairly well known phenomena in that they're what happens when the Death part of a soul breaks down. I'd really like to find out what the results are when the other four parts break down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T03:53:58-07:00","id":1142088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1141968#post1141968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case then the Omphalos were certainly established in the Time Before since it seems to be an irrevocable part of human history that can't be erased by the Exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it's been built by an Archmage via Imperium rites literally yesterday and has just allways existed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe a break in the Mind function of the soul would result in a loss to the Temenos in a way that isn't as much of a breakdown or is lateral to the Soulless and subsequent Conditions. Something like Nebuchadnezzar perhaps, where a human isn't necessarily insane but reverts to a sort of animal existence after being cut off from the rest of humanity. </div> </div> </div>Iirc that is actually what happens when you dislocate a soul of a human being using the death arcanum. The Echo Walkers legacy does it to see things that are totally not angels fallen to the abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 09-20-2017, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T04:17:37-07:00","id":1142091,"title":"","content":"I consider any retcons by archmages to be from the Time Before.<br /> <br /> The Echo Walkers use Death to nudge a soul out of alignment, which does bring the Vice to the fore, but it hardly makes them animalistic or removes their access to the Astral. Also, that's still the Death part of the soul suffering a glitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T04:30:43-07:00","id":1142096,"title":"","content":"If the Omphalous is indeed necessary for humans to perform magic then any regular archmage is going to have to come from a reality where it already existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T06:29:00-07:00","id":1142116,"title":"","content":"Two things.<br /> <br /> 1) Soulless things (like soulless people, animals, buildings, even objects) can and do leave ghosts when destroyed.<br /> <br /> 2) The Omphalamos is the Temenos Realm of Language, that being the trait separating humanity from all the other animals. It has been so since the Fall *at least* - early MtA books implied the pre-Exarch Atlanteans *built* it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T06:57:11-07:00","id":1142123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1142116#post1142116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Soulless things (like soulless people, animals, buildings, even objects) can and do leave ghosts when</div> </div> </div> </div>There is that throwing a kink into my theory. Can you elaborate on the circumstances where those other kinds of ghosts get created?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:38:05-07:00","id":1142145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1142123#post1142123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is that throwing a kink into my theory. Can you elaborate on the circumstances where those other kinds of ghosts get created?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, it only goes against the part of the theory dealing with the misfiring imprint mechanism, not against the connection between Omphalos and human Souls, so the rest of the theory is somewhat safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T11:29:35-07:00","id":1142237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1142123#post1142123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is that throwing a kink into my theory. Can you elaborate on the circumstances where those other kinds of ghosts get created?</div> </div> </div> </div>The living places (genius locii) are supposed to awaken when a sufficiently strong event takes place. It doesn't <i>have</i> to be deadly or even traumatic, but such things do provide considerable essence.<br /> Significant buildings that are destroyed sometimes leave ghosts. Significant objects of any sort might, as well.<br /> <br /> In 1e, it was pretty apparent that ghosts were a spectrum of essence not unlike the Shadow's, just one that pooled a bit apart. If you notice, the same sorts of factors that would normally lead to a spirit lead to a ghost when something is destroyed. The new version seems to want these two essences farther apart.<br /> <br /> (I still prefer running things where deathly essence simply is deathly essence so spirits of death are essentially ghosts of their primary source of essence or interact more with ghosts than other spirits. Strange mixtures that require straddling the line would be geists. Yes, in this model, the true spirit of a person (in the shadow sense) forms after they die, if at all.)<br /> <br /> Magic, of course, could be considered cheating:<br /> Death magic can make a ghost out of pretty much anything. (ectoplasm shaping, sublimating an object, making a target produce a ghost on death, et cetera)<br /> Recall that mental projections getting cut off from their host body was called out in 1e as a pretty sure way to make a ghost without Death magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 09-20-2017, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T11:32:23-07:00","id":1142238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1139469-soul-questions?p=1142145#post1142145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, it only goes against the part of the theory dealing with the misfiring imprint mechanism, not against the connection between Omphalos and human Souls, so the rest of the theory is somewhat safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that has nothing to really do with my theory on the soul. I did just come to the realization though that Mind can only create goetia, which while admittedly complex I don't think as complex as real people. Maybe the Mind part of the soul breaking down results in a breakdown of the goetia ecosystem in the Oneiros resulting in one dimensional personalities taking over the person via the Oneiros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/m